"""Colour by number on paintings, made for an older player.

A picture is split into regions, each with a number; the palette at the
bottom has one big button per number. Pick a colour, tap its regions.
- Regions still to paint are grey, lighter or darker as the colour they
  wait for, with a dark grey number; those of the chosen number are
  striped (or as chosen in Настройки) with their number bold, so they are
  easy to find. A region of another number cannot be painted. When a
  colour is done the next one with regions left is chosen, and the
  palette scrolls to it, with a soft bell and two short buzzes (the shell's haltia-press;
  haltia_paint.feedback); the header shows how far
  the picture is. With three regions or fewer of the chosen colour left,
  each gets a blue ring, seen at any zoom.
- A tap a little beside a region of the chosen number still paints it:
  a finger is wider than the smallest regions (how far beside, or only
  right on it, is a choice of Настройки).
- Numbers show once they are large enough to read; small regions show
  theirs when zoomed in.
- The buttons on the right carry drawn icons, no words, the most used on
  top: "where?" (large and blue: puts the nearest unpainted region of the
  chosen colour in the middle, zoomed in until its number reads; tapped
  again, the next one; in Настройки it can be hidden, limited to so many
  times a picture, the count left shown on it, and zoom more or less),
  undo;
  zoom in, zoom out (down to the whole picture on screen), "whole
  picture" (four corners: one tap fits the picture to the screen, the
  next one goes back to the same zoom and place); and "look" (the eye: a
  tap shows the finished picture until the next tap, or while held). A
  button that is on is blue. A drag moves the
  picture, which glides on when let go; a zoom takes a moment's glide.
  Two fingers zoom it, about where they met, where the desktop passes
  them; moving it is for one finger.
  Fingers are followed one by one (GTK's gestures follow only the
  first): a finger that does not move taps, unless another one was on
  the screen just then; one lying still for a while (a thumb holding
  the tablet, or one whose lift was lost after a palm) is left out.
- A wrong tap gets a red outline for a second and a quiet low sound, and
  no buzz: the program buzzes its own taps (buttons, a right tap) while
  the Haltia shell leaves them to it (X-Haltia-Own-Feedback, shell 2.8);
  there is no timer, no score, no ads.
- Progress is saved after every tap, so a picture can wait for tomorrow;
  the program starts on the last picture, unless it is finished.
- At a picture's end: a short tune and a longer buzz, the picture painted
  again region by region in the order it was painted (some 8 s; a tap
  skips it; Настройки can leave it out), then «Готово!» and its buttons,
  no dialog: "Сохранить в Галерею" keeps it as a PNG in Изображения/Мои
  раскраски, where Галерея (the photos program) shows it; «Посмотреть ещё
  раз», «Оригинал» (the painting itself in its place: built-in ones'
  in originals/, a downloaded one's kept beside it, an own photo) and
  «К раскраскам». A finished picture opened again shows its end.

Pictures are gzipped SVG made by pbn.py: one path per region, with its
number and the point where the number goes. The gallery (Раскраски)
shows them in sections (haltia_paint.sections), by theme or by
difficulty as chosen above it, with a button per section that scrolls
to it: first Продолжить, the pictures begun, last Готовые, the finished
ones (both in colour, their buttons beside the order's); «Наверх» comes
over the cards once they are scrolled down. To stay quick on a slow tablet (no GPU: a full redraw takes 0.75 s), the
picture is drawn in tiles at the current zoom by a thread of its own and
kept until the zoom changes; a drag only copies tiles, a zoom stretches
what is there until the new tiles come, a tap paints its region into the
tiles kept. The chosen number's regions are striped grey, or as chosen in
Настройки (⚙ in the header of the gallery and of a picture: stripes, a checker or a fill, in
grey or a bright colour; haltia_paint.highlight), as a plain
colour got lost next to painted ones. A picture's own outlines (pbn.py --ink) are drawn black over
the regions and are not painted. Progress is written a moment after the
last tap with the picture's fingerprint (data-sig), so a picture made
again starts again rather than taking another's progress; gallery
thumbnails are kept as PNG files.

It is a GTK application, io.github.haltia_de.Paint (io.github.trudenboy.Paint
before 4.0), for any desktop; on the Haltia tablet shell its GTK theme gives the
large header and dialogs (and from 2.8 it leaves the tap buzz to the
program), and it
closes the program with its own ✕; elsewhere the header has the desktop's
window buttons. Its folders were called b8k-paint before 4.0 and move on the first start.

Pictures: the built-in ones in PREFIX/share/haltia-paint/, and any photo
put into Изображения/Раскраски (JPEG or PNG; ~/Раскраски before 4.1,
moved there on the first start), which is turned into a picture of
about 300 regions in the background the first time the gallery sees it;
one that cannot be gets a line with «Ещё раз».

The gallery is built once and kept: closing a picture redraws only its
cards (again the whole gallery when it moved to Продолжить or Готовые);
the first screenful shows at once and the other cards come while
it is already in use, their thumbnails drawn in a thread.

New pictures: "+ Добавить" in the gallery header offers a picture of
one's own (those in the Pictures folder, Изображения, newest first, and
"Другая папка…": the desktop's file chooser, the portal in a Flatpak;
what was chosen there comes first next time) or a search: it searches
Wikidata for
paintings (items that are an instance of painting and have an image), by
artist, title or what is painted, in Russian as well; the pictures
themselves come from Wikimedia Commons, where every file is under a free
licence and most paintings are in the public domain. A tap on a result
shows it large with its artist, year and theme (from its genre or what
it depicts on Wikidata; a tap changes it), as it will look painted at the
chosen size of regions (a tap on it shows the painting itself), with
big numbers (no region too thin for a number read without zooming far
in; «Крупные номера», on at first) and with none, few or more of its own
black outlines kept (prints, drawings; «Контуры: нет / мало / много»). pbn.py
makes it in a process of its own at low priority, as it takes 15 to 30
seconds on the tablet, with a bar of how far it is; only one pbn.py runs
at a time (haltia_paint.convert): the preview goes before photos, and
leaving it stops its work. "Раскрашивать" keeps it in
~/.local/share/haltia-paint/downloaded/ (in the section of its theme,
own pictures among Мои фотографии) and opens it; "✕ Убрать" on its card
takes it out again. Only https requests to
wikidata.org, commons.wikimedia.org and the Wikimedia image hosts are
made.
Downloads have a 60-second deadline; search thumbnails use their own two
workers, with stale jobs cancelled when leaving the page or changing the query.
Photos and originals are decoded at display size in the worker pool;
source images above 64 million pixels are rejected. A broken picture
leaves the current page intact, and startup falls back to the gallery.
